{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","title":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":443,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","line":1014,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Myers' fundamental-group theorem]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter}\n  \\source{petersen:page-0267}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch6-myers-index, cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter, def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.3.3}\n\n  If $(M,g)$ is a complete Riemannian manifold with $\\operatorname{Ric}\\ge(n-1)k>0$,\n  then $\\operatorname{diam}(M,g)\\le\\pi/\\sqrt k$, and $(M,g)$ has finite fundamental\n  group.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases}\n  \\sketch\n  The summed sine-field variation contradicts any minimizing geodesic longer than \\(\\pi/\\sqrt{k}\\). The diameter bound follows, and the compact universal cover has a finite deck group.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Myers&#x27; fundamental-group theorem] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d6d796572732d72696363692d6469616d65746572\"></span> <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0267</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23lem%3Apet-ch6-myers-index\">↗ lem:pet-ch6-myers-index</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23cor%3Apet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter\">↗ cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23def%3Apet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound\">↗ def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:6.3.3</span></span><p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> is a complete Riemannian manifold with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k&gt;0$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k&gt;0$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {diam}(M,g)\\le \\pi /\\sqrt k$\">$\\operatorname {diam}(M,g)\\le \\pi /\\sqrt k$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> has finite fundamental group.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23rem%3Apet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases\">↗ rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases</a> \\sketch The summed sine-field variation contradicts any minimizing geodesic longer than <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi /\\sqrt{k}$\">$\\pi /\\sqrt{k}$</span>. The diameter bound follows, and the compact universal cover has a finite deck group. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-explicit-cover","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#ex:pet-ch6-punctured-sphere-infinite-pi1","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","title":"lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","label":"lem:pet-ch6-myers-index"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","title":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","label":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","title":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","label":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","title":"rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","label":"rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#ex:pet-ch6-doubly-warped-ricci-positive","title":"ex:pet-ch6-doubly-warped-ricci-positive","label":"ex:pet-ch6-doubly-warped-ricci-positive"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-ricci-simply-connected","title":"cor:pet-ch6-ricci-simply-connected","label":"cor:pet-ch6-ricci-simply-connected"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","title":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[Myers' fundamental-group theorem]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter}\n  \\source{petersen:page-0267}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch6-myers-index, cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter, def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.3.3}\n\n  If $(M,g)$ is a complete Riemannian manifold with $\\operatorname{Ric}\\ge(n-1)k>0$,\n  then $\\operatorname{diam}(M,g)\\le\\pi/\\sqrt k$, and $(M,g)$ has finite fundamental\n  group.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases}\n  \\sketch\n  The summed sine-field variation contradicts any minimizing geodesic longer than \\(\\pi/\\sqrt{k}\\). The diameter bound follows, and the compact universal cover has a finite deck group.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","title":"lem:pet-ch6-myers-index","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","title":"cor:pet-ch6-hopf-rinow-myers-diameter","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","title":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","title":"rem:pet-ch6-second-variation-special-cases","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}